/-!
# A descent situation whose index outgrows the site, and whose limit is empty

A directed inverse system of algebraic spaces over `S` with affine transition morphisms, together
with a chosen limit cone, is an `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.DescentSituation`. Its index is a
preorder in the site's own universe, and the structure imposes **no** bound on the cardinality of
that preorder.

This file exhibits such a situation whose index is as large as the site's size cutoff, whose
stages are quasi-compact quasi-separated schemes of the site, none of them affine, and whose
limit is the **empty** algebraic space, which is affine. So the statement of [Stacks, Tag 07SQ] —
an affine limit has an affine stage — is **false** when stated with no bound on the index.

It also exhibits, from the same material, a system of **affine** objects of the site with affine
transition morphisms whose limit in the site and limit in schemes disagree: the first is the
empty scheme and the second receives a morphism from the spectrum of a field, hence is not empty.
That is the exact failure of the two fields `isLimit` and `schemeIsLimit` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AffineChartSystem.LimitBridge` holding together, and it is why the index
bound of [Stacks, Tag 07SF] cannot be replaced by affineness of the limit.

## The construction

Let `K` be a field with at least `B.cutoff` elements; one exists in the site's own universe
because `B.cutoff` is a cardinal there (`wideField`). Index by `Finset K`, a directed preorder
with `B.cutoff ≤ #(Finset K)`. Every stage ring is the subring of `K` generated by a finite set,
hence countable, hence small for the cutoff whatever it is; the two systems of stages are

* the punctured planes over the stage rings, `Stacks.Refute09ZM.diagramUniv`, whose stages are
  quasi-compact, quasi-separated and **not affine** and whose transition morphisms are affine;
* the spectra of the stage rings, `Stacks.EmptyLimitCounterexample.schemeDiagramUniv`, whose
  stages are **affine**.

The base is the terminal scheme, so each stage is a scheme over the base in exactly one way.

Either system's limit in presheaves on the site is represented by the empty scheme, by the
cardinality collapse of
`Stacks.EmptyLimitCounterexample.isEmpty_cone_pt_of_mk_lt`: a morphism from the presheaf
represented by an object `Y` of the site to the vertex of a cone names a compatible family of
morphisms to the stages, hence a compatible family of ring homomorphisms from the finitely
generated subrings of `K` into `Γ(Y, ⊤)`, hence an injection of `K` into `Γ(Y, ⊤)`. But `Y` is an
object of the site, so `#Γ(Y, ⊤) ≤ 2 ^ size Y < B.cutoff ≤ #K`, the cutoff being a strong
prelimit. So no object of the site admits such a morphism unless it has no points at all, and
that is exactly what the empty algebraic space is.

The limit of the affine system *in schemes* is a different thing entirely: the stage rings sit
inside `K`, so `Spec K` is the vertex of a cone over it, and any limit of it in schemes therefore
receives a morphism from `Spec K`.

## What is and is not claimed

Nothing here bears on [Stacks, Tag 07SQ] as the Stacks Project states it, which is a statement
about a directed set in the ambient set theory and is true. What is refuted is the statement with
the index freed of the site's cutoff. The same construction at a free index *universe* is
`Stacks.Refute09ZM`; this is its cardinal form, and it is the relevant one when the index lives
in the site's own universe, where no universe gap is available.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Refute07SQ.wideField`: a field, in a cardinal's own universe, of at least that
  cardinality.
* `Stacks.Refute07SQ.siteDiagramOf`: a system of schemes of the site over the terminal base, read
  in the site, with `Stacks.Refute07SQ.systemOf` the system of algebraic spaces it represents.
* `Stacks.Refute07SQ.collapse`: the descent situation.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Refute07SQ.cutoff_le_mk_index`: the index is at least as large as the site's cutoff.
* `Stacks.Refute07SQ.isEmpty_of_hom`: an object of the site admitting a morphism to the vertex of
  a cone over the system has no points. This is the collapse, read in the site.
* `Stacks.Refute07SQ.isLimitLimitConeOf` and `Stacks.Refute07SQ.isLimitSiteLimitCone`: the cone
  with the empty algebraic space as vertex is a limit cone, in presheaves and in the site.
* `Stacks.Refute07SQ.isAffineSpace_limitCone_pt`,
  `Stacks.Refute07SQ.not_isAffineSpace_system_obj`: the limit is affine and no stage is.
* `Stacks.Refute07SQ.not_statement07SQ`: **the statement of [Stacks, Tag 07SQ] with no bound on
  the index is false.**
* `Stacks.Refute07SQ.isEmpty_isLimit_mapCone_affineSiteDiagram`: **no cone over the affine system
  in the site has an image which is a limit cone of schemes**, so affineness cannot replace the
  index bound in [Stacks, Tag 07SF].

## References

* [The Stacks Project, Tag 07SQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07SQ)
* [The Stacks Project, Tag 07SF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07SF)
* [The Stacks Project, Tag 09RH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09RH)
-/

@[expose] public section

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry AlgebraicGeometry.Space Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.Refute07SQ

/-! ### A field as large as a prescribed cardinal -/

/-- The field of rational functions in `κ` variables over the rationals: a field in the universe
of `κ` with at least `κ` elements. -/
abbrev wideField (κ : Cardinal.{u}) : Type u := FractionRing (MvPolynomial κ.out ℚ)

/-- **`wideField κ` has at least `κ` elements.** The variables are distinct in the polynomial
ring, and a domain embeds in its field of fractions. -/
theorem le_mk_wideField (κ : Cardinal.{u}) : κ ≤ Cardinal.mk (wideField κ) := by
  have hinj : Function.Injective (fun s : κ.out =>
      algebraMap (MvPolynomial κ.out ℚ) (wideField κ) (MvPolynomial.X s)) :=
    (IsFractionRing.injective (MvPolynomial κ.out ℚ) (wideField κ)).comp
      MvPolynomial.X_injective
  exact (Cardinal.mk_out κ).symm.trans_le (Cardinal.mk_le_of_injective hinj)

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u})

/-- The ground field of the counterexample: a field with at least `B.cutoff` elements. -/
abbrev ground : Type u := wideField B.cutoff

/-- The index of the counterexample: the finite subsets of the ground field, ordered by
inclusion. -/
abbrev Index : Type u := Finset (ground B)

/-- The base of the counterexample: the terminal scheme, which every big fppf site contains. -/
abbrev base : Scheme.{u} := ⊤_ Scheme.{u}

/-- **The index is at least as large as the site's cutoff**, so the counterexample is outside the
reach of [Stacks, Tag 07SF], whose hypothesis is that the index have fewer elements than the
cofinality of the cutoff. -/
theorem cutoff_le_mk_index : B.cutoff ≤ Cardinal.mk (Index B) := by
  refine (le_mk_wideField B.cutoff).trans
    (Cardinal.mk_le_of_injective (f := fun x => ({x} : Index B)) ?_)
  intro x y h
  simpa using h

/-- The stage ring at `T`: the subring of the ground field generated by a finite subset. -/
abbrev stageRing (T : Index B) : Type u := EmptyLimitCounterexample.stageUniv (ground B) T

/-- A countable type has at most `(base).size ^ ℵ₀` elements. -/
private theorem mk_le_size_pow_aleph0 (R : Type u) [Countable R] :
    Cardinal.mk R ≤ (base).size ^ Cardinal.aleph0 :=
  (Cardinal.mk_le_aleph0 (α := R)).trans
    ((Scheme.aleph0_le_size (base)).trans
      (Cardinal.self_le_power _ Cardinal.one_lt_aleph0.le))

/-- **A stage ring has at most `(base).size ^ ℵ₀` elements**, being countable. -/
theorem mk_stageRing_le (T : Index B) :
    Cardinal.mk (stageRing B T) ≤ (base).size ^ Cardinal.aleph0 :=
  mk_le_size_pow_aleph0 _

/-! ### The empty algebraic space -/

/-- The empty algebraic space, as an object of the site: the site's own empty object. -/
abbrev emptyObj : BigFppfOver B base B.contains_terminal :=
  BigFppfOver.empty B base B.contains_terminal

/-- The empty object is initial in the site. -/
def isInitialEmptyObj : IsInitial (emptyObj B) :=
  BigFppfOver.isInitialEmpty B base B.contains_terminal

/-- The underlying scheme of the empty object has no points. -/
instance isEmpty_emptyObj :
    IsEmpty ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).obj (emptyObj B)) :=
  inferInstanceAs (IsEmpty (∅ : Scheme.{u}))

/-- **An object of the site with no points is initial in the site.** Its underlying scheme is
initial among schemes, and both the size-bounded subcategory and the slice over the base inherit
that. -/
def isInitialOfIsEmptyObj {Y : BigFppfOver B base B.contains_terminal}
    (hY : IsEmpty ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).obj Y)) : IsInitial Y :=
  Over.isInitialOfIsInitialLeft (isInitial_schemeBelow B (@isInitialOfIsEmpty _ hY))

/-- There is at most one morphism of the site out of an object with no points. -/
theorem subsingleton_hom_of_isEmpty {Y Z : BigFppfOver B base B.contains_terminal}
    (hY : IsEmpty ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).obj Y)) :
    Subsingleton (Y ⟶ Z) :=
  ⟨fun f g => (isInitialOfIsEmptyObj B hY).hom_ext f g⟩

/-- The morphism of the site from an object with no points to the empty object. -/
def toEmptyObj (Y : BigFppfOver B base B.contains_terminal)
    (hY : IsEmpty ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).obj Y)) :
    Y ⟶ emptyObj B :=
  (isInitialOfIsEmptyObj B hY).to _

/-- **There is at most one morphism of the site to the empty object.** A morphism to a scheme
with no points makes its source have none either, and out of such an object there is at most one
morphism. -/
instance subsingleton_toEmptyObj (Y : BigFppfOver B base B.contains_terminal) :
    Subsingleton (Y ⟶ emptyObj B) := by
  refine ⟨fun f g => ?_⟩
  have hY : IsEmpty ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).obj Y) :=
    Function.isEmpty ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).map f).base
  exact (subsingleton_hom_of_isEmpty B hY).elim f g

/-! ### A system of schemes of the site over the terminal base, and its limit

A diagram `E` of schemes all of which the site contains, read in the site over the terminal base,
whose limit in presheaves and in the site is the empty object as soon as a cone over `E` with few
enough global sections at its vertex has no points at all. -/

section Diagram

variable (E : (Index B)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Scheme.{u}) (hE : ∀ T, B.Contains (E.obj T))

/-- The diagram `E`, read in the site over the terminal base: the objects are contained in the
site by `hE`, and each carries exactly one morphism to the terminal scheme. -/
def siteDiagramOf : (Index B)ᵒᵖ ⥤ BigFppfOver B base B.contains_terminal :=
  Functor.toOver ((schemeSizeBelow B.cutoff).lift E hE) (B.obj B.contains_terminal)
    (fun _ => ObjectProperty.homMk (terminal.from _))
    (fun _ => by apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext; exact terminalIsTerminal.hom_ext _ _)

/-- The underlying scheme of the object of `siteDiagramOf B E hE` at `T` is `E.obj T`. -/
@[simp] theorem toScheme_siteDiagramOf_obj (T : (Index B)ᵒᵖ) :
    (BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).obj ((siteDiagramOf B E hE).obj T) =
      E.obj T := rfl

/-- The underlying morphism of schemes of `(siteDiagramOf B E hE).map g` is `E.map g`. -/
@[simp] theorem toScheme_siteDiagramOf_map {T T' : (Index B)ᵒᵖ} (g : T ⟶ T') :
    (BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).map ((siteDiagramOf B E hE).map g) =
      E.map g := rfl

/-- The system of algebraic spaces: the presheaves represented by the objects of the diagram. -/
def systemOf : (Index B)ᵒᵖ ⥤ (BigFppfOver B base B.contains_terminal)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u :=
  siteDiagramOf B E hE ⋙ yoneda

/-- The cone over the diagram in the site with the empty object as vertex. -/
def siteLimitCone : Cone (siteDiagramOf B E hE) where
  pt := emptyObj B
  π :=
    { app := fun T => (isInitialEmptyObj B).to ((siteDiagramOf B E hE).obj T)
      naturality := fun _ _ _ => (isInitialEmptyObj B).hom_ext _ _ }

/-- The cone over the system with the empty algebraic space as vertex. -/
def limitConeOf : Cone (systemOf B E hE) where
  pt := yoneda.obj (emptyObj B)
  π :=
    { app := fun T => yoneda.map ((isInitialEmptyObj B).to ((siteDiagramOf B E hE).obj T))
      naturality := fun T T' g => by
        have h : (isInitialEmptyObj B).to ((siteDiagramOf B E hE).obj T) ≫
              (siteDiagramOf B E hE).map g
            = (isInitialEmptyObj B).to ((siteDiagramOf B E hE).obj T') :=
          (isInitialEmptyObj B).hom_ext _ _
        simp only [Functor.const_obj_obj, Functor.const_obj_map, Category.id_comp, systemOf,
          Functor.comp_map, ← yoneda.map_comp, h] }

/-- The vertex of `limitConeOf B E hE` is the presheaf represented by the empty object. -/
@[simp] theorem limitConeOf_pt : (limitConeOf B E hE).pt = yoneda.obj (emptyObj B) := rfl

/-- The morphism of the site that an object `Y` and a morphism `yoneda Y ⟶ s.pt` name at the
stage `T`: the Yoneda embedding of the site being fully faithful, a morphism of representable
presheaves is a morphism of the site. -/
def legOfHom (s : Cone (systemOf B E hE)) (Y : BigFppfOver B base B.contains_terminal)
    (x : yoneda.obj Y ⟶ s.pt) (T : (Index B)ᵒᵖ) : Y ⟶ (siteDiagramOf B E hE).obj T :=
  Yoneda.fullyFaithful.preimage (x ≫ s.π.app T)

/-- The morphisms `legOfHom B E hE s Y x T` are compatible with the transition morphisms of the
diagram in the site. -/
theorem legOfHom_comp (s : Cone (systemOf B E hE))
    (Y : BigFppfOver B base B.contains_terminal) (x : yoneda.obj Y ⟶ s.pt)
    {T T' : (Index B)ᵒᵖ} (g : T ⟶ T') :
    legOfHom B E hE s Y x T ≫ (siteDiagramOf B E hE).map g = legOfHom B E hE s Y x T' := by
  refine Yoneda.fullyFaithful.map_injective ?_
  rw [Functor.map_comp, legOfHom, legOfHom, Functor.FullyFaithful.map_preimage,
    Functor.FullyFaithful.map_preimage]
  change (x ≫ s.π.app T) ≫ (systemOf B E hE).map g = x ≫ s.π.app T'
  rw [Category.assoc, s.w g]

/-- A morphism from a representable presheaf to the vertex of a cone over the system, read as a
cone over the diagram of schemes with the representing object's underlying scheme as vertex. -/
def coneOfHom (s : Cone (systemOf B E hE)) (Y : BigFppfOver B base B.contains_terminal)
    (x : yoneda.obj Y ⟶ s.pt) : Cone E where
  pt := (BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).obj Y
  π :=
    { app := fun T => (BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).map
        (legOfHom B E hE s Y x T)
      naturality := fun T T' g => by
        change 𝟙 _ ≫ (BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).map
              (legOfHom B E hE s Y x T')
            = (BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).map
                (legOfHom B E hE s Y x T) ≫
              (BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).map
                ((siteDiagramOf B E hE).map g)
        rw [Category.id_comp, ← Functor.map_comp, legOfHom_comp] }

/-- **The collapse, read in the site.** Suppose every cone over `E` whose vertex has fewer global
sections than the ground field has elements has a vertex with no points — which is what the
cardinality collapse of a system of stage rings says. Then an object of the site admitting a
morphism from its representable presheaf to the vertex of a cone over the system has no points:
an object of the site has fewer than `B.cutoff` global sections, the cutoff being a strong
prelimit, and the ground field has at least that many elements. -/
theorem isEmpty_of_hom
    (hcol : ∀ s : Cone E, Cardinal.mk Γ(s.pt, ⊤) < Cardinal.mk (ground B) → IsEmpty s.pt)
    (s : Cone (systemOf B E hE)) (Y : BigFppfOver B base B.contains_terminal)
    (x : yoneda.obj Y ⟶ s.pt) :
    IsEmpty ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).obj Y) := by
  refine hcol (coneOfHom B E hE s Y x) ?_
  calc Cardinal.mk Γ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).obj Y, ⊤)
      ≤ 2 ^ ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).obj Y).size :=
        Scheme.mk_sections_le_two_pow_size _ _
    _ < B.cutoff := B.cutoff_isStrongPrelimit Y.left.property
    _ ≤ Cardinal.mk (ground B) := le_mk_wideField _

/-- The comparison morphism from the vertex of a cone over the system to the empty algebraic
space: at every object of the site its value is the unique morphism to the empty object, which
exists because an object at which the vertex has a point has no points. -/
def liftToEmpty
    (hcol : ∀ s : Cone E, Cardinal.mk Γ(s.pt, ⊤) < Cardinal.mk (ground B) → IsEmpty s.pt)
    (s : Cone (systemOf B E hE)) : s.pt ⟶ (limitConeOf B E hE).pt where
  app Y := ↾(fun g => toEmptyObj B Y.unop (isEmpty_of_hom B E hE hcol s Y.unop
    (yonedaEquiv.symm (show s.pt.obj (op Y.unop) from g))))
  naturality _ Y' _ := by
    ext _
    exact (subsingleton_toEmptyObj B Y'.unop).elim _ _

/-- **The cone with the empty algebraic space as vertex is a limit cone in presheaves.** Every
object of the site at which the vertex of a competing cone has a point has no points, hence is
initial in the site, so the comparison morphism exists at every object and is unique there. -/
def isLimitLimitConeOf
    (hcol : ∀ s : Cone E, Cardinal.mk Γ(s.pt, ⊤) < Cardinal.mk (ground B) → IsEmpty s.pt) :
    IsLimit (limitConeOf B E hE) where
  lift s := liftToEmpty B E hE hcol s
  fac s T := by
    ext Y g
    exact (subsingleton_hom_of_isEmpty B (isEmpty_of_hom B E hE hcol s Y.unop
      (yonedaEquiv.symm (show s.pt.obj (op Y.unop) from g)))).elim _ _
  uniq s m _ := by
    ext Y _
    exact (subsingleton_toEmptyObj B Y.unop).elim _ _

/-- **The vertex of any cone over the diagram in the site has no points**: its identity names a
morphism from its own representable presheaf to the vertex of the cone's image in presheaves. -/
theorem isEmpty_cone_pt_univ
    (hcol : ∀ s : Cone E, Cardinal.mk Γ(s.pt, ⊤) < Cardinal.mk (ground B) → IsEmpty s.pt)
    (c : Cone (siteDiagramOf B E hE)) :
    IsEmpty ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).obj c.pt) :=
  isEmpty_of_hom B E hE hcol (yoneda.mapCone c) c.pt (𝟙 _)

/-- **The cone with the empty object as vertex is a limit cone in the site.** -/
def isLimitSiteLimitCone
    (hcol : ∀ s : Cone E, Cardinal.mk Γ(s.pt, ⊤) < Cardinal.mk (ground B) → IsEmpty s.pt) :
    IsLimit (siteLimitCone B E hE) where
  lift c := toEmptyObj B c.pt (isEmpty_cone_pt_univ B E hE hcol c)
  fac c _ := (subsingleton_hom_of_isEmpty B (isEmpty_cone_pt_univ B E hE hcol c)).elim _ _
  uniq c _ _ := (subsingleton_toEmptyObj B c.pt).elim _ _

end Diagram

/-! ### The punctured planes: the descent situation refuting Stacks 07SQ -/

/-- The stage at `T` of the punctured system: the punctured plane over the stage ring. -/
abbrev stageScheme (T : Index B) : Scheme.{u} :=
  (Refute09ZM.diagramUniv.{u, u} (ground B)).obj (op T)

/-- **Every stage of the punctured system is an object of the site**: it is an open subscheme of
the affine plane over a countable ring, and a countable ring is small for the cutoff of any big
fppf site, the cutoff being uncountable. -/
theorem contains_stageScheme (T : (Index B)ᵒᵖ) :
    B.Contains ((Refute09ZM.diagramUniv.{u, u} (ground B)).obj T) := by
  have hcount : Countable (affinePlaneRing (stageRing B T.unop)) :=
    Function.Injective.countable (f := AddMonoidAlgebra.coeff)
      fun a b h => by cases a; cases b; simp_all
  have hplane : B.Contains (affinePlane (stageRing B T.unop)) :=
    Scheme.size_Spec_lt_of_mk_le B.aleph0_lt_cutoff B.cutoff_isStrongPrelimit _
      B.contains_terminal (mk_le_size_pow_aleph0 _)
  have hopen := Scheme.size_lt_of_isOpenImmersion
    (Refute09ZM.stageOpenUniv.{u, u} (ground B) T).ι hplane
  exact hopen

/-- The collapse for the punctured system. -/
theorem collapse_punctured (s : Cone (Refute09ZM.diagramUniv.{u, u} (ground B)))
    (hs : Cardinal.mk Γ(s.pt, ⊤) < Cardinal.mk (ground B)) : IsEmpty s.pt :=
  Refute09ZM.isEmpty_cone_pt_of_mk_lt s hs

/-- The punctured system, read in the site over the terminal base. -/
abbrev puncturedSiteDiagram : (Index B)ᵒᵖ ⥤ BigFppfOver B base B.contains_terminal :=
  siteDiagramOf B (Refute09ZM.diagramUniv.{u, u} (ground B)) (contains_stageScheme B)

/-- The punctured system, as a system of algebraic spaces. -/
abbrev puncturedSystem :
    (Index B)ᵒᵖ ⥤ (BigFppfOver B base B.contains_terminal)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u :=
  systemOf B (Refute09ZM.diagramUniv.{u, u} (ground B)) (contains_stageScheme B)

/-- **The counterexample, as a descent situation.** Every field of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.DescentSituation` is discharged: the stages are algebraic spaces over the
terminal base, quasi-compact and quasi-separated, the transition morphisms are affine, and the
chosen cone is limiting with the empty algebraic space as vertex. Its index is `Finset` of a field
at least as large as the site's cutoff. -/
def collapse :
    DescentSituation B base B.contains_terminal B.contains_terminal (Index B) where
  system := puncturedSystem B
  algebraicSpace _ := isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B base B.contains_terminal _
  transition_affine f :=
    isAffineHom_yoneda_map_of_isAffineHom ((puncturedSiteDiagram B).map f)
      (Refute09ZM.isAffineHom_diagram_map_univ (ground B) f)
  quasiCompact T :=
    isQuasiCompact_yoneda_of_compact B base B.contains_terminal
      ((puncturedSiteDiagram B).obj (op T))
      (inferInstanceAs (CompactSpace (stageScheme B T)))
  quasiSeparated T :=
    isAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated_of_isQuasiSeparatedScheme B base B.contains_terminal
      (yoneda.obj ((puncturedSiteDiagram B).obj (op T))) B.contains_terminal
      ⟨(puncturedSiteDiagram B).obj (op T),
        inferInstanceAs (QuasiSeparatedSpace (stageScheme B T)),
        ⟨Functor.RepresentableBy.yoneda _⟩⟩
  limitCone := limitConeOf B _ (contains_stageScheme B)
  isLimit := isLimitLimitConeOf B _ (contains_stageScheme B) (collapse_punctured B)
  limitAlgebraicSpace := isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B base B.contains_terminal _
  base := ∅

/-- The system of the descent situation `collapse B` is the punctured system. -/
@[simp] theorem collapse_system : (collapse B).system = puncturedSystem B := rfl

/-- **The limit of the descent situation is an affine algebraic space**: it is the empty scheme,
which is affine. -/
theorem isAffineSpace_limitCone_pt :
    IsAffineSpace B base B.contains_terminal (collapse B).limitCone.pt :=
  ⟨emptyObj B, inferInstance, ⟨Iso.refl _⟩⟩

/-- **No stage of the descent situation is an affine algebraic space.** A representable presheaf
is affine only if its representing object is, the Yoneda embedding of the site being fully
faithful, and no punctured plane is affine. -/
theorem not_isAffineSpace_system_obj (T : Index B) :
    ¬ IsAffineSpace B base B.contains_terminal ((collapse B).system.obj (op T)) := by
  rintro ⟨W, hW, ⟨e⟩⟩
  have hiso : (puncturedSiteDiagram B).obj (op T) ≅ W := Yoneda.fullyFaithful.preimageIso e
  have := hW
  have haff := IsAffine.of_isIso
    ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).mapIso hiso).hom
  exact Refute09ZM.not_isAffine_punctured (stageRing B T) haff

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 07SQ] with no bound on the index is false.**

The statement, at the terminal base: for a directed preorder `I` in the site's universe and a
descent situation over `I` whose limit is an affine algebraic space, some stage beyond the
distinguished index is an affine algebraic space. The counterexample is the system of punctured
planes over the finitely generated subrings of a field with at least `B.cutoff` elements: its
limit is the empty algebraic space, which is affine, its distinguished index is the least one, and
no stage is affine.

What the Stacks Project states carries no such counterexample: there the index is a directed set
in the ambient set theory, and the limit of the affine charts of a stage stays inside the site.
The bound on the index is what expresses that here, as in
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.hasLimit_of_isAffine_of_sizeBound`. -/
theorem not_statement07SQ :
    ¬ ∀ {I : Type u} [Preorder I] [IsDirected I (· ≤ ·)]
        (D : DescentSituation B base B.contains_terminal B.contains_terminal I),
        IsAffineSpace B base B.contains_terminal D.limitCone.pt →
        ∃ i : I, D.base ≤ i ∧
          IsAffineSpace B base B.contains_terminal (D.system.obj (Opposite.op i)) := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨T, -, hT⟩ := h (collapse B) (isAffineSpace_limitCone_pt B)
  exact not_isAffineSpace_system_obj B T hT

/-! ### The spectra of the stage rings: affineness does not replace the index bound -/

/-- **Every spectrum of a stage ring is an object of the site**, the stage rings being
countable. -/
theorem contains_specStageRing (T : (Index B)ᵒᵖ) :
    B.Contains ((EmptyLimitCounterexample.schemeDiagramUniv.{u, u} (ground B)).obj T) :=
  Scheme.size_Spec_lt_of_mk_le B.aleph0_lt_cutoff B.cutoff_isStrongPrelimit _
    B.contains_terminal (mk_stageRing_le B T.unop)

/-- The collapse for the system of spectra of the stage rings. -/
theorem collapse_affine (s : Cone (EmptyLimitCounterexample.schemeDiagramUniv.{u, u} (ground B)))
    (hs : Cardinal.mk Γ(s.pt, ⊤) < Cardinal.mk (ground B)) : IsEmpty s.pt :=
  EmptyLimitCounterexample.isEmpty_cone_pt_of_mk_lt s hs

/-- The system of spectra of the stage rings, read in the site over the terminal base: a system
of **affine** objects of the site with affine transition morphisms. -/
abbrev affineSiteDiagram : (Index B)ᵒᵖ ⥤ BigFppfOver B base B.contains_terminal :=
  siteDiagramOf B (EmptyLimitCounterexample.schemeDiagramUniv.{u, u} (ground B))
    (contains_specStageRing B)

/-- Every object of the affine system has affine underlying scheme. -/
instance isAffine_affineSiteDiagram_obj (T : (Index B)ᵒᵖ) :
    IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).obj
      ((affineSiteDiagram B).obj T)) :=
  inferInstanceAs (IsAffine ((EmptyLimitCounterexample.schemeDiagramUniv.{u, u} (ground B)).obj T))

/-- Every transition morphism of the affine system is affine on underlying schemes. -/
instance isAffineHom_affineSiteDiagram_map {T T' : (Index B)ᵒᵖ} (g : T ⟶ T') :
    _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineHom
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).map ((affineSiteDiagram B).map g)) :=
  inferInstanceAs (_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineHom
    ((EmptyLimitCounterexample.schemeDiagramUniv.{u, u} (ground B)).map g))

/-- The inclusion of a stage ring into the ground field. -/
def stageInclusion (T : Index B) : stageRing B T →+* ground B :=
  (Subring.subtype _).comp (EmptyLimitCounterexample.stageEquivUniv (ground B) T).toRingHom

/-- **The spectrum of the ground field is the vertex of a cone over the affine system**: every
stage ring sits inside the ground field, compatibly with the transition homomorphisms, which are
the inclusions of one subring in another. -/
def specGroundCone : Cone (affineSiteDiagram B ⋙
    BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal) where
  pt := Spec (CommRingCat.of (ground B))
  π :=
    { app := fun T => Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (stageInclusion B T.unop))
      naturality := fun T T' g => by
        change 𝟙 _ ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (stageInclusion B T'.unop))
            = Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (stageInclusion B T.unop)) ≫
              Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
                (EmptyLimitCounterexample.stageMapUniv (ground B) (leOfHom g.unop)))
        rw [Category.id_comp, ← Spec.map_comp, ← CommRingCat.ofHom_comp]
        refine congrArg Spec.map (congrArg CommRingCat.ofHom (RingHom.ext fun x => ?_))
        simp [stageInclusion] }

/-- **No cone over the affine system in the site has a limit cone of schemes for its image.**

The vertex of *any* cone over the system in the site has no points, by the collapse — no limit
hypothesis is needed for that. But a limit cone in schemes receives a morphism from `Spec` of the
ground field, which does have a point. So for a system of affine objects of the site with affine
transition morphisms — the shape of the system of affine charts of a stage of a descent situation
— the two assertions

* the cone is a limit cone in the site, and
* its image is a limit cone in schemes

can never hold together. They are the fields `isLimit` and `schemeIsLimit` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AffineChartSystem.LimitBridge`, so there is no `LimitBridge` for a chart
system with an index this large: affineness of the limit — here the limit is the empty algebraic
space, which is affine — does not replace the bound on the index in
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.hasLimit_of_isAffine_of_sizeBound`. -/
theorem isEmpty_isLimit_mapCone_affineSiteDiagram (c : Cone (affineSiteDiagram B)) :
    IsEmpty (IsLimit ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).mapCone c)) := by
  refine ⟨fun hsch => ?_⟩
  have hempty :=
    isEmpty_cone_pt_univ B _ (contains_specStageRing B) (collapse_affine B) c
  have hpoint : Nonempty (Spec (CommRingCat.of (ground B))) :=
    inferInstanceAs (Nonempty (PrimeSpectrum (ground B)))
  have hmap := hsch.lift (specGroundCone B)
  have hemptyK : IsEmpty (Spec (CommRingCat.of (ground B))) :=
    have : IsEmpty ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B base B.contains_terminal).mapCone c).pt := hempty
    Function.isEmpty hmap.base
  exact hemptyK.elim hpoint.some

end Stacks.Refute07SQ

